# Health and mana on the left wrist (#116, D-029, D-037): two bars, red towards the elbow and blue towards the
# hand, on the inner side of the left wrist of the full body (#36); read by raising the wrist to the face like
# a watch, faded out when it turns away. While they are on the wrist the HUD's orbs are not drawn.
# Needs a first-person save (TRAPS.md: level 10's conversation camera is nowhere near the body):
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence wrist-vitals -Save mvp-new-game
@sim idle
@save mvp-new-game
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert vr.body.left.posed eq true

# The idle rig holds the left grip upright, the palm facing right: the bars are on the wrist (the orbs step
# aside); how much of them shows depends on how the inner wrist meets the eyes
@assert vr.wrist.shown eq true
@assert vr.wrist.health eq 1
@assert vr.wrist.mana eq 1

# The left hand in front of the chest, right of the middle, the knuckles to the right, so the forearm runs
# across the view (elbow on the left); the head looks at it. First the back of the hand up (the palm down,
# the thumb towards the player): the inner wrist faces away from the eyes, nothing is drawn
vr-sim head rot -20 -45 0
vr-sim hand left pos 0.12 -0.3 -0.3
vr-sim hand left rot 180 0 -90
@frames 15
@assert vr.body.left.posed eq true
@assert vr.wrist.facingDeg gt 80
@assert vr.wrist.alpha eq 0
@shot wrist-away

# The watch pose: the palm turned to the eyes, the thumb up - fully visible, drawn into both eyes. The hand
# sits further right and nearer than the pose above, the palm yawed 10 degrees towards the head (#304): the
# roll-aware arm's relaxed pole (down, back, a little out) and its elbow swing put the elbow behind the wrist
# at (0.12, -0.3, -0.3), so the forearm ran away from the eyes (along 0.36 / -0.58 / 0.73); here the
# shoulder-hand line runs to the right and the forearm with it. Further right the forearm runs across the view
# even more but the inner wrist turns away from the eyes (0.3 / -0.3 / -0.25: facing 59 degrees); the yaw
# brings the palm back to the eyes, more of it tips the bars' "up" and the palm's normal off their limits
# (-105: normal z -0.71) - a sweep of positions and yaws on the simulated headset
vr-sim hand left pos 0.25 -0.3 -0.25
vr-sim hand left rot -100 90 0
@frames 15
@assert vr.body.left.posed eq true
@assert vr.wrist.shown eq true
@assert vr.wrist.facingDeg lt 50
@assert vr.wrist.alpha eq 1
# The forearm runs to the right (health, towards the elbow, is the left bar); the bars fill upwards (engine
# y is down), towards the thumb, across the forearm (measured on #36's arm at the old pose: along 0.71 /
# -0.56 / 0.43, across -0.62 / -0.78 / 0.00 - the forearm rises 34 degrees, so "up" leans left with it;
# on #304's arm here: along.x 0.59, across.y -0.70, facing 47); the inner wrist faces back towards the eyes
# (normal z -0.90 on #36's arm, -0.74 on #304's)
@assert vr.wrist.along.x gt 0.5
@assert vr.wrist.across.y lt -0.6
@assert vr.wrist.normal.z lt -0.7
@remember drawn vr.wrist.drawnViews
@frames 5
@assert vr.wrist.drawnViews ge {drawn+10}
@shot wrist-full

# Damage and spent mana: the fractions follow the player's pools. The picture is judged on the captures, not
# by @diff: two still shots of this pose already differ by 2.2 (the idle animation), as much as the bars do
specialfx heal -9
specialfx mana -6
@frames 10
@assert vr.wrist.health lt 0.9
@assert vr.wrist.mana lt 0.9
@shot wrist-hurt

# Half turned away (the palm turned 30 degrees further from the eyes): fading
vr-sim hand left rot -100 90 -30
@frames 10
@assert vr.wrist.alpha gt 0
@assert vr.wrist.alpha lt 1
@shot wrist-fading

# Without a left controller the arm goes back to the engine and the orbs come back
vr-sim hand left off
@frames 10
@assert vr.body.left.posed eq false
@assert vr.wrist.shown eq false
@shot orbs-back
@diff wrist-hurt orbs-back gt 0.15 quad
vr-sim hand left on
@frames 10
@assert vr.wrist.shown eq true

@assert errors eq 0
